  "note": "The multi-call proposal, and the whole reason ADR 0019 exists: the second call names the track id the first call's result returned. Under dry runs that call is refused `track_unknown`, because the track was minted into a document that was thrown away.\n\nHand-written from the shape of `one-answer.json`, which is a real recorded exchange (M3 PR 5). Nothing here was recorded: recording a turn costs a paid call to OpenRouter, and CLAUDE.md #7 says nothing calls a paid service without the user's confirmation, which this pull request did not have. Every field but `choices` and `usage.prompt_tokens` is copied from the recorded response, so what the SDK parses is the shape a provider really sends: `provider`, `native_finish_reason`, `service_tier`, `moderation` and the rest. `usage.prompt_tokens` is set generously on purpose \u2014 the loop refuses a response whose token count says the provider dropped the prompt (ADR 0022 \u00a73), and a hand-written 68 would have tripped it. The live run behind OPENROUTER_API_KEY is what replaces a hand-written transcript with a recorded one.",
